      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Bounded RH verification is a staged certificate rather than a list of apparent roots: controlled zeta evaluation supplies values, phase normalization turns critical-line localization into real sign tests, a separate total-zero count checks completeness, Turing averaging stabilizes that check, and batched evaluation scales the same architecture to large ranges.",
