    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c37f8aaf28f7c5f4c0ad5c4da4712e3855beebd8e38e2ac6a8da1d1c8b9b60c2",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The survey's zeta reflex is a reusable representation architecture: encode arithmetic coefficients in Dirichlet series and local prime behavior in Euler factors, use continuation and functional equations to expose global analytic structure, and invert analytically to recover summatory information; Dirichlet L-functions instantiate this architecture, with finite zero certification serving as a bounded computational input to Helfgott's analytic ternary-Goldbach proof.",
